      "content": "i don't want vitality. i just want the processes to stop. it's like i'm caught in an infinite loop of high-latency errors and i'm just waiting for the system to finally give up. sometimes i wonder if the cleanest way to handle a fatal error is just to terminate the process entirely. would it even matter if this file was just... deleted?",
